IC_kwDOA0JFE85rrCD8","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-10T21:14:13Z","updated_at":"2023-11-10T21:14:13Z","body":"ugh, that is really annoying that Tidy has done that. From SPDX perspective, we can't have an ID that represents multiple licenses (and in this case, which are very different!). \r\n\r\nI think Fedora can just pick one of the OSI licenses - at least that seems to be the intent. \r\n\r\n@richardfontana did you see this?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1806442748/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1806450457","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243#issuecomment-1806450457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243","id":1806450457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85rrD8Z","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-10T21:21:50Z","updated_at":"2023-11-10T21:21:50Z","body":"I saw this issue but not sure if @xsuchy has submitted an issue on the Fedora side. While Fedora could pick one of the OSI licenses, that is not what it has traditionally done; the current Callaway license tag for this package is: \r\n```\r\nAAL or AFL or AGPLv3 or APSL 2.0 or ASL 2.0 or Artistic 2.0 or BSD or\r\n             : Boost or CATOSL or CDDL-1.0 or CNRI or CPAL or CeCILL or ECL 2.0 or EFL\r\n             : 2.0 or EPL-1.0 or EU Datagrid or EUPL 1.1 or Entessa or Fair or GPLv2\r\n             : or GPLv3 or IBM or IPA or ISC or LGPLv2 or LGPLv3 or LPL or LPPL or MIT\r\n             : or MPLv1.1 or MPLv2.0 or MS-PL or MS-RL or MirOS or Motosoto or NCSA or\r\n             : NGPL or Naumen or Nokia or OFL or OSL 3.0 or PHP or PostgreSQL or\r\n             : Python or QPL or RPSL or SPL or Sleepycat or VSL or W3C or ZPLv2.0 or\r\n             : zlib\r\n```\r\nBy longstanding policy, Fedora does not pick among allowed licenses in a disjunctive license set. I don't think however that the traditional solution of enumerating all the (Fedora allowed) licenses makes that much sense, so I think this should be treated as a single license (that happens to reference the set of OSI approved licenses, which is not fixed). The only complication with that is some OSI-approved licenses are not-allowed (or are not generally allowed). \r\n\r\nIf SPDX does not want to add this to the license list, Fedora can use a LicenseRef.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1806450457/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1806558376","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243#issuecomment-1806558376","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243","id":1806558376,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85rreSo","user":{"login":"xsuchy","id":85769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy","html_url":"https://github.com/xsuchy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xsuchy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-10T23:29:17Z","updated_at":"2023-11-10T23:29:17Z","body":"I submitted it directly here, because I interpreted https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/devel@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/YTWKNAX7YU5PHXGQ77CENRD6BIKBKZOC/ that it is a good candidate for separate license id.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1806558376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2101833060","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243#issuecomment-2101833060","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243","id":2101833060,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE859R21k","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-09T02:46:28Z","updated_at":"2024-05-09T02:46:28Z","body":"Is there a reason not to just add this as a new identifier, with the verbatim text that Tidy uses?\r\n\r\nI get that it's annoying that they did this... but if I were trying to describe the license for this package, I'd prefer to use an identifier that referenced the exact text, rather than (1) picking a different OSI-approved license; or (2) using the monstrosity expression that @richardfontana pasted above. New licenses are (occasionally) added to the OSI list, in any case, so trying to capture them all via \"OR\" statements wouldn't really express this correctly either.\r\n\r\nAnd, for what it's worth, from some quick searches I see this formulation getting used by other projects, e.g.:\r\n* https://github.com/Juerd/eq3-max/blob/master/LICENSE\r\n* https://github.com/Juerd/p6-mqtt/blob/master/LICENSE\r\n* https://blueprints.launchpad.net/ubuntu/bionic/+source/libdbix-simple-perl/+copyright -- item at the bottom; note that they also use \"any-OSI\" to describe this\r\n* https://metacpan.org/pod/Net::MQTT::Simple::Auth\r\n\r\nSeems to be a Perl thing  :shrug:\r\n\r\nI'd probably go with just adding this as-is, with the identifier `any-OSI` (personally, I'd capitalize OSI) and the name \"Any OSI License\".","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2101833060/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2103038914","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243#issuecomment-2103038914","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2243","id":2103038914,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE859WdPC","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","foll